WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.228
Part four. The cover letter.

00:00:02.528 --> 00:00:06.337
A generic cover letter is worse than sending none at all,

00:00:06.337 --> 00:00:09.010
because everybody can spot the template.

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:12.218
A good one names what the company actually does,

00:00:12.218 --> 00:00:15.359
and connects it to what you have actually done.

00:00:15.359 --> 00:00:18.900
That is an hour of work for every single application,

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.175
which is why almost nobody writes one every time.

00:00:22.175 --> 00:00:23.511
Here, it is one tap.

00:00:23.811 --> 00:00:26.490
Open a saved job, and tap generate.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.103
It reads the posting properly first.

00:00:29.403 --> 00:00:32.408
Then it goes and researches the company itself.

00:00:32.708 --> 00:00:36.413
What comes back is written for that role, at that company.

00:00:36.713 --> 00:00:38.448
Same regional formats.

00:00:38.448 --> 00:00:42.866
Pick yours, then download it, or edit the wording first.

00:00:43.166 --> 00:00:44.201
One thing left.

00:00:44.201 --> 00:00:49.171
Did you know the app can fill in the employer's form for you, and apply?

00:00:49.171 --> 00:00:50.620
That is the last one.

